# docs / UML / commit activation thresholds

Lane: ao.fleet.dynamic.0f5da8ca8544
Orchestrator: ao-fleet-conductor-leaf-0f5da8ca8544

This file defines the fail-closed activation thresholds for the docs, UML, and
commit sidecars.

## Preconditions

- The proposed action stays inside its declared typed support.
- The action has a concrete state transition to describe.
- The action does not create semantic, legal, proof, or promotion authority.
- Protected ESD surfaces remain untouched.
- Verification evidence exists for any state claimed as complete.

## Thresholds

### Docs

Activate a docs update only when at least one of these state changes occurs:

- a public contract changes;
- a workflow state changes;
- an operator-visible behavior changes;
- a promotion or abstention boundary changes;
- a verification result changes the documented state.

Do not update docs for a refactor that preserves all documented behavior.

### UML

Activate UML only when system topology changes materially.

A material topology change is one of:

- a component or service is added or removed;
- a dependency direction changes;
- an authority boundary changes;
- a persistent data-flow edge changes;
- a runtime ownership boundary changes.

Do not activate UML for text changes, local refactors, naming changes, or
unchanged topology.

### Commit

Activate a publish/checkpoint commit sidecar only when all of these conditions
hold:

- the lane has a complete bounded result;
- deterministic verification for that result has passed;
- the result is ready to be consumed by another lane or reviewed as a stable
  checkpoint;
- no unresolved local edit is being hidden by the checkpoint.

Do not create a publish/checkpoint commit merely because work occurred.

## Invariants

- Docs, UML, and commit activation are independent decisions.
- One activated sidecar does not activate the others.
- No sidecar can promote candidate state into authoritative state.
- No sidecar can bypass review, verification, or promotion gates.
- No threshold may be lowered by an unrelated lane.
- noTypedMeet independence is preserved across all sidecars.

